# Implementation Plan - Universal SQL Optimization & Safety

This plan upgrades SQAuto to handle **MySQL, SQLite, and Postgres** uncompresssed dumps up to 2GB+, while implementing a safe "Wipe" mechanism for fresh scans.

## Architectural Note (For User)

> [!NOTE]
> **Where is your data?**
> Your data **is stored on Supabase**. When we run the restoration, the VM acts as a "high-speed pipe" that reads your 1.8GB file and streams it directly to your Supabase PostgreSQL database. 
> 
> The reason you don't see "Migrations" is that migrations are only for the *app's* structure (like the Jobs list). The **tables** from your SQL dump are inserted directly into the database. I will help you verify this by showing you how to find them in the Supabase Table Editor.

## User Review Required

> [!CAUTION]
> **Safe Wiping**: Since your App (the Job list) and your Staging Dump share the same database, we cannot simply "Delete Everything" because it would delete the SQAuto app itself!
> 
> **The Solution**: I will implement a **Selective Wipe**. It will identify all tables that are NOT part of the SQAuto system (anything except the `jobs` table) and drop only those before starting a new scan. This gives you a clean slate while keeping the app alive.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Infrastructure (Multi-SQL Tooling)

#### [MODIFY] [Dockerfile](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/docker/Dockerfile)
- Install `pgloader` and `mariadb-client` dependencies. `pgloader` is the industry standard for converting MySQL data into Postgres in real-time.

### 2. Backend - Universal Restorer & Safe Wipe

#### [MODIFY] [service.py](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/services/dump_restore/service.py)
- **Signature Detection**: Read the first 2KB of `.sql` files to detect if it's MySQL (`-- MySQL dump`) or Postgres (`-- standard postgres`).
- **Selective Wipe**: Before restoration, query the database for all user tables and `DROP` them, excluding the system `jobs` table.
- **pgloader Dispatcher**: If a MySQL dump is detected, automatically generate a `pgloader` command to migrate the data into your Supabase Postgres instance.

### 3. Backend - Live Monitor (5-Card Update)

#### [MODIFY] [service.py](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/services/schema_profiler/service.py)
- Enhance the monitoring heartbeat to report **Storage Footprint** in MB and **Row Counts** every 5 seconds.

### 4. UI - Industrial Dashboard

#### [MODIFY] [page.tsx](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/apps/web/src/app/page.tsx)
- Connect all 5 cards (TABLES, ROWS, DATA EXTRACTED, DUPLICATE DATA, READINESS) to the live data stream.

## Open Questions

- **Timeout Check**: With 1.8GB passing through to Supabase, the process might take 45-90 minutes. I have set the limit to **1 hour**. Should we increase it to **2 hours** just to be absolutely safe for your largest files?

